  Four ES modules, each independently understandable and testable:

  ┌────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────┐
  │   Module   │                                Responsibility                                │     Depends on      │
  ├────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mstorage.js[39m │ Serialize/deserialize the task array to a [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m key. Handles absent   │ the injected        │
  │            │ and corrupt data.                                                            │ storage object      │
  ├────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mtasks.js[39m   │ Pure functions over a task array: [38;5;153maddTask[39m, [38;5;153mtoggleDone[39m, [38;5;153meditTask[39m, [38;5;153mdeleteTask[39m, │ nothing             │
  │            │  [38;5;153msetDueDate[39m. No I/O, no DOM.                                                 │                     │
  ├────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mstore.js[39m   │ Owns current state. Applies a [38;5;153mtasks.js[39m operation, persists via [38;5;153mstorage.js[39m,   │ [38;5;153mstorage.js[39m,         │
  │            │ computes the change event, notifies subscribers.                             │ [38;5;153mtasks.js[39m            │
  ├────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mrender.js[39m  │ Given state, rebuild [38;5;153m<main>[39m. Wires DOM events to [38;5;153mstore[39m calls.                │ [38;5;153mstore.js[39m            │
  └────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────┘

  Data flow is a single loop, one direction:

  user action → store.apply(op, args)
                  ├─ newState = op(state, args)     (pure)
                  ├─ storage.save(newState)
                  ├─ changes = diff(state, newState)
                  └─ notify(subscribers, newState, changes)
                           └─ render.js rebuilds <main>

  The [1mchange-event chokepoint[0m is the [38;5;153mdiff[39m line. It emits [38;5;153m{taskId, field, oldValue, newValue, timestamp}[39m per changed
  field. Nothing consumes it yet except a subscriber that logs to console — deliberately, so the shape gets exercised.
  When notifications become their own spec, they register as a second subscriber and no existing module changes.

  [38;5;153mtasks.js[39m being pure is what makes the unit tests worth having: they're plain function calls, no DOM, no fakes.

  Does this look right so far?

